\ audio: the sequencer's note-length words over the (sequence-note) (sequence-chord) (sequence-rest) primitives

\ a note length as the exact numerator and denominator of a fraction of a whole note
: length>fraction ( length -- numerator denominator ) float>exact dup numerator swap denominator ; internal

\ queue a note on the current instrument, starting where that instrument's previous note ended
: sequence-note ( pitch length -- ) length>fraction (sequence-note) ;

\ queue several pitches starting together, then advance the instrument by one length
: sequence-chord ( pitches length -- ) length>fraction (sequence-chord) ;

\ advance the current instrument by a length without sounding
: sequence-rest ( length -- ) length>fraction (sequence-rest) ;
